Bibliography database (BibTeX with abntex2cite).

Writing rules for new entries:
- accented letters in author and organization names use LaTeX commands, for
  example Guimar{\~a}es, so BibTeX can convert them to uppercase;
- titles in sentence case; protect acronyms and proper names with braces;
- page ranges with a single hyphen (462-471), as in the template;
- events follow NBR 6023:2018: organization holds the event name and
  conference-number, conference-year and conference-location complete it.

Only cited entries appear in the reference list.

Style options read by abntex2-alf.bst (loaded in config/packages.tex).

@abnt-options{ifce-options,
  abnt-cite-style = "(Author, YEAR)",
  abnt-emphasize  = "\textbf",
  abnt-etal-list  = 0,
  key             = "aaaa"
}

